| AC-008 | SCN-031 | Corresponding AGDF task-plan-review, clean-implementation-review, code-review and qa-gate on current bound run/sources/results | Selected current run; no reused superseded review authority | T-001 preparation; implementation and verification evidence; Desktop gap disposition from T-010; deliberate later approvals separate | Current review owners; QA sole decision owner; maintainer for human decisions | Current TP_REVIEW.md; CLEAN_IMPLEMENTATION_REVIEW.md; CR.md; QA_REPORT.md; permitted next action | Route normalized gaps; QA revise/block where required proof is missing, no assumed UAT/OR or publication approval |

### Targeted and full verification command inventory

Use actual npm scripts already maintained by the repository, extending their owned tests where the approved implementation requires it:

- npm run test:release-qualification and node scripts/native-probes/release-evidence-test.mjs for candidate, handoff, lifecycle and strict old/new evidence contracts.
- npm --prefix packages/cli run test:release-workflows plus node --test scripts/ci-plan-test.mjs for publication dependencies, full per-lane command multiset and timeout preservation.
- npm --prefix packages/cli run test:release-version-coherence, test:distribution-profile-history, test:release-bump, test:package-contents and the existing runtime-integrity/package suites through their canonical chains.
- Affected lifecycle/consent/host-command/cache tests through packages/cli's existing scripts; actual platform suites remain in ordinary CI.
- npm run test:host-compatibility, npm run compatibility:record, npm run compatibility:check and inspected generated/public/readiness output for report assurance and exact labels.
- npm run build, npm --prefix packages/cli run release:prepare, npm run verify:ci and git diff --check for the current complete source snapshot. If an existing sealed artefact has a formatting issue, route correction through its owner; do not edit sealed bytes to make the command green.
- When an authorized staged/ref snapshot exists, npm run verify:commit (index) or npm run verify:commit -- --ref <exact-ref> proves that exact exported snapshot. This plan does not itself stage, commit or push.

Do not create another executable inventory to replace canonical npm chains. Capture baseline/current normalized command arrays from testInventory/ciJobs exported by scripts/ci-plan.mjs as evidence only and prove every original command remains assigned in each ordinary lane. Add new deterministic tests to the current canonical chains so planning fails closed on unknown/unclassified commands. Workflow structural checks and actual CI success are separate; record the SHA and available job results for any remote claim, without inventing a fresh run or automatically triggering protected/model workflows.

## Planning Decisions

| Decision | Source | Status | Resolution | Owner |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Original Desktop evidence recovery and targeted-case boundary | SD: Original evidence recovery and targeted execution | resolved | T-010 begins with SCN-019 original-source inventory and per-fact applicability. SCN-020 through SCN-025 assess six exact Desktop cases on final candidate. Preserve the three reported passes per host and every unknown field; execute only a specifically justified missing fact/case when safe prerequisites exist. Missing access/identity remains an explicit qualification gap with named action, never a fabricated result or blanket retest | Evidence reviewer; maintainer as original observation owner; actual Desktop executor |
| Executable coverage and ordering | SD: Executable cases and validation order | resolved | Eleven tasks and 31 scenarios map all eight PRD criteria and eight SD decisions. T-001 precedes changes; generation precedes consumers; T-009 finalizes/recomputes candidate; T-010 validates available original/current evidence; T-011 evaluates actual reviews/QA. Every Test Plan row specifies route, environment, permissions, evidence and unavailable action | TP author and verification owner |
| Mandatory versus optional execution | TP | resolved | Only both Desktop targets and their six records feed mandatory release eligibility. Claude Windows CLI remains separate historical/optional evidence; Codex Windows/Linux CLI stays unqualified outside mandatory scope. Retain optional CLI safeguards and complete ordinary Linux/Windows regression inventory/timeouts | Native policy and CI owners |
| Exact environment resolution point | TP | resolved | Actual Desktop app/OS/model/session/runtime is recovered from original primary references first and frozen in reviewed tuples before qualified acceptance. Claude Windows is known context; Codex OS remains unknown until evidenced. Values are observations at T-010, not new product/design choices; missing facts leave qualification pending under approved scope | Evidence reviewer and original/native executor |
| Final candidate and CLI reuse | TP | resolved | Preserve original candidate 830d8b94 CLI bytes and review them with original predicates. New policy/source changes produce a new candidate; exact recomputation is required for current applicability. No mandatory CLI rerun is introduced because of the Desktop scope | Candidate and native evidence owners |
| Baseline, ownership and bounded execution | TP | resolved | Verify actual released 0.14.5 integrity and use supported owned-stale repair, foreign sentinels and fresh loaded identity. Preserve existing helper/job limits and stop unsafe ownership/capture/cleanup; no limit increase or broad deletion | Lifecycle and native execution owners |
| VCS, remote and human decision boundary | TP | resolved | Prepare reviewable local code/evidence and exact handoff. No automatic stage/commit/push/tag, publication, credential transfer, new remote access or external messaging. Record a missing clean-ref/access prerequisite rather than inventing execution; later QA/UAT/OR decisions remain exact and separate | Release preparation owner and maintainer |

The above resolves the two SD later_tp decisions exactly once. Runtime values and evidence availability are checked at their named execution resolution points because they are not supplied current facts; the approved product/design already defines the safe missing-result behavior. No unresolved acceptance or architecture decision is delegated to a test executor. If a concrete gap changes scope, design or required executability beyond these approved stop paths, stop affected work and use the existing normalized clarification/source owner rather than silently editing approved sources.

## 4. Brownfield Scope

Before implementation, T-001 inspects current approved UR/PRD/SD, source revision receipt/archive, current Review and retained changes/results; canonical hostSupport/validation/generator; release-policy/candidate/observation/handoff/lifecycle helpers; Codex and Claude native probe parsers and optional workflow; complete publication dependency graph; compatibility manifest/native projection/rendering; release/profile/package owners and ordinary CI plan/inventory. Record BROWNFIELD_ANALYSIS.md through the current internal-step writer before CD+Tests.

Preserve the unrelated core-model-handoff-simplification-20261015-01 directory and any later foreign work. Capture exact baseline paths and source digests; do not reset, clean or stage another work line. Never hand-edit RUN_STATE, MASTER_BACKLOG, approved source bytes, source bindings, receipts or seals. Historical source/quality records retain history but supply no renewed fulfillment or approval.

## 5. Out Of Scope

Publication, tags, marketplace submission, automatic VCS actions, remote services or messaging, blanket credentials/trust/approval, active-host replacement, product/UI redesign, Core gate changes, experimental-host removal/qualification, Codex CLI Windows/Linux qualification, fabricated native traces/tuples and weakened ownership/evidence/cleanup/history/payload/time-limit checks. This plan does not claim any native case or new CI run passed.

## 6. Risks And Blockers

Both Desktop handchecks are documented but exact Desktop identities/candidate/primary captures remain unknown. Preparation and implementation can produce a reviewable revised matrix while those qualification obligations remain pending; final overall qualification and publication stay blocked until required proof is current and complete. Report that condition through SCN-019/026/029/031, not as a passed test or clean delivery closeout.

The policy/probe migration changes candidate identity, so historical evidence may be useful without qualifying the final candidate. Missing original files, unsafe Desktop isolation, inaccessible remote capture, baseline integrity failure, unknown ownership, false cleanup, inventory omission, partial publication dependencies or timeout are concrete blockers for their affected scenario. Preserve independent authorized progress and original failures. Any needed relaxation or change of product/design scope returns to the earliest existing source owner with renewed approval.

No clean final shared commit, host credentials, fresh Desktop capture, original missing identity or completed human acceptance is asserted. QA alone decides pass/revise/block from actual current reports; later human acceptance cannot be inferred from this plan or a successful parser test.

## 7. Next Step

Present this exact plan for a new deliberate Approval: TP. That approval permits post-TP implementation-preparation Brownfield Analysis, then scoped implementation and checks when the analysis supports them. Record actual CD+Tests and current reviews/QA through their owners. Keep unresolved evidence and human UAT/OR/publication boundaries explicit; no final release action follows automatically.

## AGDF Approval Summary (de; source=en)

- Ziel: Die genehmigte Desktop-Matrix umsetzen und den Abschluss mit nachvollziehbaren Aufgaben, Prüfungen und offenen Nachweisen vorbereiten.
- Plan: Elf Aufgaben decken Bestandsprüfung, kanonische Policy, Kandidatenbindung, strenge Desktop-Nachweise, Übergabe/Import, Upgrade/Wiederherstellung, Veröffentlichungssperre, Berichte, Paketprüfung und Reviews ab.
- Abdeckung: 31 Szenarien ordnen alle acht PRD-Kriterien und acht SD-Entscheidungen konkreten Aufgaben, erwarteten Ergebnissen, Ausführungswegen und Nachweisen zu. Alle normalen CI-Tests und bestehenden Zeitlimits bleiben erhalten.
- Desktop-Nachweise: Sechs Pflichtfälle umfassen Sitzung, Upgrade und Wiederherstellung für Codex Desktop und Claude Desktop. Zuerst vorhandene Originalbelege zuordnen; nur konkrete Lücken begründen gezielte neue Beobachtungen in sicherem Testbereich. Gemeldete Handprüfungen bleiben erhalten, unbekannte Identitäten bleiben unbekannt.
- CLI und Support: Fünf Windows-Claude-CLI-Fälle bleiben beim ursprünglichen Kandidaten und werden getrennt geprüft. Codex CLI unter Windows/Linux bleibt unqualifiziert und außerhalb der Pflichtmatrix; optionale Probes bleiben erhalten. Copilot/OpenCode bleiben experimentell mit ihren Tests.
- Ablauf: Nach TP-Freigabe zuerst Implementierungsvorbereitung, dann abgestimmte Quelländerungen und Paket-/Regressionstests. Anschließend sauberen finalen Kandidaten prüfen, tatsächliche Desktop-Belege bewerten und aktuelle Reviews/QA erstellen. Kein vorhandener Erfolg wird auf die neue Kandidatenidentität umetikettiert.
- Grenzen: Fehlende Desktop-Versionen, Modelle, Kandidaten, Primärbelege oder sicherer Rechnerzugriff bleiben konkrete Qualifikationslücken. Keine lokalen Claude-Zugangsdaten verlangen, fremde Profile ändern, pauschalen Tests wiederholen oder Freigaben ableiten. Unvollständige Pflichtbelege verhindern weiterhin Gesamtqualifikation und Veröffentlichung.
- Nächster Schritt: Neue TP-Freigabe öffnet Bestandsanalyse und danach die zulässige Umsetzung. Keine automatischen Commits, Pushes, Tags, Veröffentlichung oder weiteren menschlichen Abnahmen.
